
Defects report (16 defect )

Defect 1: Admin user has Compliance Approval button enabled
Preconditions:
User is logged in with an Admin role.
A shipment with pending compliance decision (e.g. HOT-EXCURSION) is open.
Steps to Reproduce:
Login as Admin user.
Navigate to a shipment that requires compliance decision.
Open the Compliance tab.
Actual Result:
“Approve compliance” button is enabled and clickable.
Expected Result:
According to RBAC and Figma, only authorized roles should see the button enabled. Confirm if Admin is intentionally allowed. If not, the button should be disabled or hidden.
Reproducibility: Always
Severity: Major
Priority: High
Business/Risk Rationale: Incorrect permission assignment can lead to unauthorized compliance decisions, creating audit and regulatory risk.

Defect 2: Warehouse user has Compliance Approval button enabled
Preconditions:
User is logged in with a Warehouse role.
A shipment requiring compliance decision is open.
Steps to Reproduce:
Login as Warehouse user.
Open a shipment with pending compliance.
Go to Compliance tab.
Actual Result:
“Approve compliance” button is enabled.
Expected Result:
Warehouse role should not have permission to approve compliance (button should be disabled or hidden) as per RBAC design.
Reproducibility: Always
Severity: Critical
Priority: Critical
Business/Risk Rationale: Warehouse users approving compliance violates segregation of duties and can invalidate cold-chain compliance records.

